# Not uploaded to Vercel at all. Distinct from excludeFiles in vercel.json,
# which trims the function bundle after upload — this trims the upload itself.
.venv/
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/

# Worth knowing if you ever add an entry here to fix a build: this file trims
# a *CLI upload* only. Deploys from the GitHub integration clone the repo and
# never consult it, so excluding a file here does not keep it out of those
# builds.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
public/

# pytest configuration, and nothing else — see the file. It has to be kept out
# of the upload entirely rather than merely out of the function bundle, because
# it breaks the build before bundling is reached: Vercel's Python runtime is
# uv-based, and uv treats any pyproject.toml as a project manifest. This one
# has no [project] table, so `uv lock` fails and the deploy dies with
# "No `project` table found in: /vercel/path0/pyproject.toml".
#
# Excluding it is what makes the runtime fall back to requirements.txt, which
# is the file this project actually declares its dependencies in. Adding a
# [project] table instead would work too and is the worse fix — it would give
# the repo a second, competing dependency list for uv to resolve, and
# tests/test_requirements_sync.py exists precisely because one duplicate list
# is already one too many.
pyproject.toml

# Scanned insurer PDFs the overlay schemas point at ARE needed at runtime, so
# forms/ is deliberately absent from this list. Same for extension/, which the
# download endpoint zips on request.
